### Configure V8 max semi-space size for Node.js

Source: https://github.com/nodejs/node/blob/v22.20.0/doc/api/cli.md

This option sets the maximum semi-space size for V8's scavenge garbage collector in MiB. Adjusting this value can improve throughput for Node.js workloads at the cost of increased memory consumption, as the young generation size is three times the semi-space size. Benchmarking different values is crucial for optimal configuration depending on the application's workload and system memory limits.

```bash
for MiB in 16 32 64 128; do
    node --max-semi-space-size=$MiB index.js
done
```

--------------------------------

### Set V8 max old space size with Node.js

Source: https://github.com/nodejs/node/blob/v22.20.0/doc/api/cli.md

This option configures the maximum memory size for V8's old memory section in MiB. Increasing this limit can reduce the frequency of garbage collection, but setting it too high may lead to excessive memory consumption. It is recommended to leave some memory for other uses to prevent swapping.

```bash
node --max-old-space-size=1536 index.js
```

--------------------------------

### Get V8 Heap Space Statistics in Node.js

Source: https://github.com/nodejs/node/blob/v22.20.0/doc/api/v8.md

This method returns an array of objects, each detailing statistics for a specific V8 heap space (e.g., 'new_space', 'old_space', 'code_space'). Each object includes `space_name`, `space_size`, `space_used_size`, `space_available_size`, and `physical_space_size`. The structure and availability of these spaces may vary between V8 versions.

```json
[
  {
    "space_name": "new_space",
    "space_size": 2063872,
    "space_used_size": 951112,
